     [38;5;246msessionStorage; cleared when the tab closes. The value is non-authoritative — used for showing who's logged in and
[39m     [38;5;246mstamping client-side logs. Lowest risk.[39m
  [38;5;246m2.[39m Across browser restarts
     [38;5;246mlocalStorage; survives until explicitly cleared. Convenient for 'remember me', but persists identity on shared [39m
     [38;5;246mmachines and needs an explicit clear-on-logout path.[39m
  [38;5;246m3.[39m Server needs to see it
     [38;5;246mA cookie, so it rides along on requests to the API. This makes it part of the auth surface and needs [39m
     [38;5;246mSecure/HttpOnly/SameSite decisions — significantly larger scope.[39m
  [38;5;246m4.[39m In-memory only
     [38;5;246mA module-level session object, no persistence at all. Survives navigation within the SPA but not a page reload. [39m
     [38;5;246mSmallest security surface.[39m
